entries.en:
Through Samadhi, one can attain the state of Yama (restraint);
Through Samadhi, one can attain the eight Siddhis;
Indeed, for those who abide in Samadhi and Yama,
Samadhi and Yama themselves will be attained.

In the manner of Sadaashiva, the immutable Agama;
In the manner of Sivagathi, the Punnai where bees dwell;
In the manner of the sacred dance and the scriptural words;
Thus, the Pure One becomes universal in the sacred hall.

He who entered the mind, causing the seven worlds to rejoice;
He who entered the earth, supporting the great firmament;
He who entered wrath, causing the eight directions to tremble;
He who entered the wilderness, his place is called the North.

The hand that flung away, saying 'Begone!' (to impurities);
The flower-like hand that embraced, saying 'Come!' (to ascetics);
The golden hand, in fitting form, indicating 'That' (the Supreme);
This perfected, sacred state is indeed the divine fire, the 'Ma' syllable.
